    <p>In 2026, the legal landscape of Bosnia and Herzegovina is defined by a deep divide between international aspirations and internal political gridlock. Same-sex partnerships still cannot be legally registered in the country as of early 2026. The "Law on Same-Sex Partnership" has been stalled since 2023, primarily due to the Federal Ministry of Health intentionally blocking the appointment of experts to the drafting committee. This blockade has left hundreds of couples without basic legal protections regarding inheritance and medical decisions.</p>

